  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 200°C/180°C fan-forced. Cut mini flour tortillas into 2cm strips.\n• Finely chop brown onion. Finely grate or crush garlic.\n• Grate carrot. Roughly chop tomato. Pick and roughly chop mint. Drain and rinse chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60f9225c73ae8755b109d371/step-370e1248.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide tortillas between the lined oven trays, arranging in a single layer.\n• Brush (or spray) with olive oil and season.\n• Bake until lightly golden and crisp, 8-10 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60f9225c73ae8755b109d371/step-b69fc9ae.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, heat butter and a drizzle of olive oil in a large saucepan over medium-high heat.\n• Cook onion until softened, 3-4 mins. Add ginger paste, garlic, Bengal curry paste (see ingredients) and tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1-2 mins.\n• Add a drizzle more olive oil and add carrot, tomato and chickpeas. Cook, stirring, until slightly softened, 2-3 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60f9225c73ae8755b109d371/step-4d0c8c9d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Reduce heat to medium and add the salt and coconut milk to the pan. Stir to combine.\n• Cook until veggies have softened and the dhal has thickened, 4-5 mins. Add a splash of water if the dhal looks dry.\n• Season and divide between bowls. Sprinkle with mint. Serve with flatbread dippers.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/60f9225c73ae8755b109d371/step-d0bb24f9.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
